# English captions (seconds in the ORIGINAL recording NAF002.mp3). *word* = shown in gold.
# Cleaned from the TurboScribe translation for the Shorts. Lines in “quotes” are read from the book Nizam-ul-Amal-e-Fuqara.
# The full dars needs the rest of the transcript (from 27:55) before its captions are complete.
CAPTIONS = [
    (0.14, 71.36, 'Everyone has come to meet me today, family and friends together, and there is great joy. Whatever small doubt is in your heart, throw it away. The arrangement of the world is in the hands of the One to whom it belongs. Allah knows best.'),
    (72.92, 147.72, '*Dhikr al-anbiya min al-ibadah*: remembering the prophets is a kind of worship. And remembering the *righteous* wipes away sins: they are forgiven. In sha Allah we have begun this dars again; this is the second session.'),
    (148.60, 197.36, "In sha Allah, from page 11 we will read the chapter on *Tawbah*, repentance. A'udhu billahi min ash-shaytan ir-rajeem. Bismillah ir-Rahman ir-Raheem."),
    (198.22, 205.00, 'The title is *Tawbah*, repentance. Bismillah ir-Rahman ir-Raheem.'),
    (205.00, 219.10, "“When a person wants to walk the path of Allah, he first *regrets* his past negligence and wrongdoing, and asks Allah's forgiveness.”"),
    (249.34, 264.18, '“He turns to Allah with his *heart*, and promises Allah that he will not disobey Him again.”'),
    (265.12, 288.20, "“If he has violated the rights of Allah's servants, he makes it up to them; and where it cannot be made up, he asks the people's *forgiveness*.”"),
    (288.28, 313.40, "This is the *reality of repentance*: to ask Allah's forgiveness for your sins, to promise to walk the straight path from now on, and to forgive others their wrongs."),
    (331.86, 338.10, '“Repentance is a quality of the *heart*.” Repentance, repentance, repentance…'),
    (338.12, 346.14, "No, it is not like that: “I am a sinner, what can I do?” and slapping your own face. Don't do this."),
    (348.14, 366.80, 'So what is repentance? It is a quality of the heart, not of the *hands*. Look: he slapped his own face and thought he had repented. What is the *effect* of repentance? That is the question.'),
    (459.83, 471.39, "“He is the One who accepts *repentance* from His servants and pardons their sins.” The Qur'an."),
    (475.51, 485.21, "By repentance *all sins* are forgiven, and a person becomes as if he had just been born from his mother's womb."),
    (486.57, 501.49, "How great repentance is! That is why, whatever work or duty you begin, after A'udhu billah and Bismillah, first *repent*. Then say Bismillah and begin."),
    (503.05, 515.85, '“Remember: a human being is the name of the union of the *soul* and the *body*.” See how clearly the master explains it.'),
    (517.51, 532.03, 'See how clearly he explains, how he teaches. Remember: a human being is the union of the *soul* and the *body*.'),
    (534.69, 545.41, '“The body is reformed by *Shariat* and *Tariqat*.”'),
    (545.41, 555.40, 'Shariat is to pray, to fast, to perform Hajj, to pay Zakat. All of this is Shariat.'),
    (557.35, 567.51, 'And what is Tariqat? To build a *connection* with Allah and His Messenger ﷺ. All of this is Tariqat.'),
    (570.52, 588.00, 'Remember: a human being is the union of the soul and the body, and the body is reformed by *Shariat* and *Tariqat*.'),
    (589.30, 591.96, '“The soul is reformed by *Haqiqat* and *Marifat*.”'),
    (593.10, 618.86, 'In the reforming of the soul, what is there? Haqiqat: Allah, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, the last Prophet, the angels, the whole order of creation. These hidden, inner things belong to the soul.'),
    (619.42, 622.64, 'We have to know them. We have to gain this *knowledge*.'),
    (623.38, 656.64, "The things of the soul cannot be seen; we come to know them through knowledge. We have not seen with our eyes, but through the *Qur'an* and the *Ahadith* we have come to know Allah, and that the Prophet ﷺ is the last Prophet."),
    (658.28, 674.44, '“It is obvious that the body will ask for its *needs*: eating, drinking, clothing, fulfilling the rights of the wife.”'),
    (675.64, 680.86, "Eating, drinking, clothing, fulfilling the rights of one's wife."),
    (682.20, 687.76, 'Pay attention: “The body is a *horse*.”'),
    (688.58, 695.80, "If you don't feed the horse, it will sit down. If you feed it too much, it becomes *unruly*."),
    (699.46, 724.85, 'MashaAllah. “The owner should *feed* the horse, and make it *run*.” Stand in the middle and make it run around you.'),
    (725.81, 734.99, "Don't let it sit idle, but take care of its rest. After eating and drinking, the horse starts to *play up*."),
    (737.93, 767.57, "It lifts its front legs and won't let you ride; it runs at you to bite. So he cut down its grain and fodder, and made it *run* a lot."),
    (773.33, 784.83, 'He tired it out on the road, and once it was tired, its *mischief* came to an end.'),
    (789.02, 863.70, 'Remember: be content with *little food*; eating too much is a fault. Overeating makes a person lazy and useless, and he begins to intend evil. After repentance, the nafs wants to turn back to what it gave up. See what teaching this is! Keeping away from evil deeds is *Taqwa*; that is why Taqwa is needed.'),
    (864.26, 870.76, '*Innallaha yuhibbul-muttaqeen*: surely Allah loves those who have Taqwa.'),
    (873.56, 886.46, '“It is clear that the *sinner* is afraid: that is fear. But the righteous are not afraid…”'),
    (888.64, 911.22, "“…they are in *awe* of Allah's Glory and Majesty.”"),
    (916.58, 957.60, "The sinner is afraid; that is fear. But the pious are in *awe* of Allah's Glory and Majesty. This is *Khashiyat-Allah*, awe of Allah."),
    (970.24, 1044.91, "Of one righteous man it was said: even if he had no fear of Allah, he would never have disobeyed Him. Such is the nature of the pious: they cannot disobey Allah. When all *good* is in Allah's hands, it is useless to expect good from others."),
    (1044.91, 1071.51, 'Some Muslims go to those who do not believe in Allah and ask them for help. They are *ungrateful*.'),
    (1072.21, 1082.27, "“A Muslim's faith rests between *fear* and *hope*.”"),
    (1083.31, 1106.33, 'Hope is to expect good from Allah; fear is to be afraid. He is Allah, *Qadir-e-Mutlaq*, the All-Powerful. We should stay in awe, and stay humble.'),
    (1108.21, 1123.23, '“But the *young* should fear sin, and the *old* should have hope in the mercy of Allah.”'),
    (1125.43, 1199.85, 'Allah is *Qadir-e-Mutlaq*: He does whatever He wills. At night, at half past one or two, Hazrat would get up to pray and say: “Call Azam.” Those serving him took turns, two at a time; they would come for me, and I would go to him at once and talk with him to make him *happy*.'),
    (1199.85, 1274.16, 'I would tell him incidents I had heard from Huzoor, and remind him of being *content with Allah*. It made him happy and had a great effect. That is why he loved me so much, MashaAllah, and taught me everything.'),
    (1274.16, 1348.56, "In his last days, as I sat serving him, he called me *“Azam Jah!”* I prostrated and wept in my heart: Ya Allah, he called me Azam Jah! In those days the royal family were called “Jah”; Azam Jah was the title of the Nizam's son."),
    (1348.84, 1415.58, "Later others too began to call me Azam Jah, MashaAllah. Let me finish: the faith of a Muslim is between *fear* and *hope*. The young should fear sin, and the old should hope for Allah's mercy, so they can give their life to their Lord happily. What a lesson!"),
    (1417.74, 1435.80, 'Once I was asked to come to a big house. Hazrat used to come there and teach on Sundays. I went and sat in front of him.'),
    (1447.56, 1459.54, "He said: “Do you know my *tasawwur*?” I said: “I don't know.”"),
    (1461.34, 1476.66, 'He said: “Do this. Hold my *picture* in your mind. Look at me in the picture.”'),
    (1477.46, 1496.58, "That's it. I began from there, and within a few days my *eyes opened*. Otherwise it is such a long book: muraqaba, then kashf."),
    (1497.34, 1518.66, '“Do you know my tasawwur? Picture me; look at me in the picture.” And at once, my eyes *opened*.'),
    (1519.64, 1594.56, "I don't have much *kashf*. Just a while ago, for 45 minutes, *Maula Ali* was present in my house. A girl came and said: give the fatiha of *Maula Mushkil Kusha*. Allahu Akbar!"),
    (1602.37, 1668.00, 'The fatiha was given. Maula stood leaning by the wall, looking at me. Then *Qadir Piya* came, in love with Maula. Did you see all this? Allahu Akbar!'),
]
